Right, on reading the Makefile[1] I found the entry
        .if defined(WITH_MENUCOLORS)
        PATCHFILES+=    nh343-menucolor.diff
        PATCH_SITES+=   http://bilious.homelinux.org/~paxed/nethack/
        PATCH_DIST_STRIP=       -p1
        CFLAGS+=        -DMENU_COLOR_REGEX_POSIX
        .endif
        .if defined(WITH_HPMON)
        PATCHFILES+=    hpmon.diff
        PATCH_SITES+=   http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nh/ \
                        ${MASTER_SITE_LOCAL:S|%SUBDIR%|koitsu|}
        PATCH_DIST_STRIP=       -p1
        CFLAGS+=        -DHPMON
        .endif

So I compile NetHack via
        # make -C /usr/ports/games/nethack34-nox11 -DWITH_MENUCOLORS -DWITH_HPMON \
        install clean

Workz great! :D
But now I think it's good to use the statusline patch[2] and the coloured
walls and floor patch[3]. Patch shows an error again...

So my question again: What do I wrong? Do I have to copy the source code in
a special directory before running patch? Could I change the Makefile[1] on
my computer to add these patchs (not a question of possibility but of
approval)?

